${tool_bullets}

## Layout

```
src/${package}/
  core/<tool>.py   pure logic, one module per tool, no I/O (edit these)
  models.py        TOOL_NAMES and TOOL_SCHEMAS (compared by scripts/check_contracts.py)
  server.py        thin MCP layer from stitch_common.mcp_app
tests/
  unit/ property/ contract/   fast tests (no network)
  test_smoke_stdio.py         starts the server over stdio, lists tools, calls one
```

## Implementing a tool

1. Write `core/<tool>.py::run(params) -> Out`. Raise `stitch_common.tooling.ToolFailure` for
   expected failures (`INFEASIBLE`, `NOT_FOUND`, ...). Return `Outcome(data, warnings=...,
   data_sources=[...])` to report provenance details.
2. Delete the matching `test_stub_*` assertion in `tests/unit/test_core.py` and add real tests.
3. Add each new third-party library to `THIRD_PARTY.md` in the same commit.

## Run

```
uv sync --all-packages
uv run python -m ${package}.server --stdio                 # stdio (Kiro, Brain)
uv run python -m ${package}.server --http --port 8000      # streamable HTTP, GET /healthz
uv run pytest organs/${organ}
uv run python scripts/check_contracts.py
```

`STITCH_MODE=demo` (default) must work offline from `data/demo/`; `live` may use the network and
falls back to demo with a warning.
